NoPrune -- NoPrune option for pushFwd
*************************************

Description
===========

This is an optional argument for the *note pushFwd: pushFwd, function. Its
default value is false, which means that the presentation of a pushed forward
module is pruned by default. If NoPrune is set to true, then the prune calls in
pushFwd are turned off.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R5=QQ[a..e]                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R5                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R6=QQ[a..f]                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = R6                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M=coker genericMatrix(R6,a,2,3)                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = cokernel | a c e |                                                      |
|              | b d f |                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|                              2                                              |
|o3 : R6-module, quotient of R6                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : G=map(R6,R5,{a+b+c+d+e+f,b,c,d,e})                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = map (R6, R5, {a + b + c + d + e + f, b, c, d, e})                       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : RingMap R6 <-- R5                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : notpruned = pushFwd(G,M,NoPrune => true)                                |
